## 4. Theorem

**Three-Graph First-Order Joint Coefficient Lift Theorem.** The exact selected
`4H` degree-six marked Fermat map embeds in the same selected gamma completion
as the two primitive-H maps through the unique displayed Hensel lifts of
`rho` and `mu`. Its eta9 restriction derivative has rank 74. The full
three-component derivative has rank 126, and the complete first-order defect
of the fixed coefficient lift lies in its image. Therefore there exists one
global correction `delta_F` such that

```text
F_joint = F_Q + 101 delta_F mod 101^2
```

restricts to zero on all three unchanged selected graph maps. Direct
substitution verifies every one of the 168 restriction rows.

**Proof.** Reconstruct the degree-six target in the quartic coordinate ring
and verify its Fermat identity in `R_2`. Restrict each of the 249 displayed
eta9 coefficient basis vectors to the three graphs, reducing respectively by
the two lifted sheet equations and the quartic relation. Exact row reduction
gives ranks `26`, `26`, `74` and stacked rank `126`. The augmented matrix is
consistent. Substitution of the emitted RREF solution into the original eta9
equation makes all three reduced restrictions zero modulo `101^2`. QED.

